From 6f76c7ff39e5ef93e011c2402a8e1d0bfdc932bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:51:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add KWALIFY-START.bat / KWALIFY-STOP.bat for simple local
 server control

KWALIFY-START: checks Node/npm, loads the existing .env (values never printed),
refuses to start a second copy, refuses to touch a foreign process holding the
port, checks PostgreSQL reachability (TCP only, never starts or modifies it),
runs npm ci only if node_modules is missing, builds only when backend sources
are newer than backend/dist, then runs node backend/dist/server.js (what npm
start runs) in its own window and waits for /api/readyz.

KWALIFY-STOP: finds the server via a recorded PID (verified by start time and
command line) or the node server.js process owning the port, sends Ctrl+C to
its console (the server's existing graceful SIGINT shutdown), waits up to 130s,
and only offers a force-stop of that verified PID if it does not exit.

Existing launchers (start.bat, start-kwalify.bat, stop-kwalify.bat, ...) are
unchanged. Different file names are used because START-KWALIFY.bat would be the
same file as start-kwalify.bat on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
